================================================================================
## Explorer: search results are marked with a visible halo
================================================================================

Context:
After an Explorer search, the entity that matched the search value looked
like every other node. The seed highlight set borderColor / borderSize, but
Sigma's default circle program ignores per-node borders, so only a small size
bump was visible.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   - New _drawSeedHalos(): a DOM layer over the canvases with one pulsing
     ring per highlighted seed.
   - Ring position and size come from getNodeDisplayData,
     framedGraphToViewport and scaleSize, and are redrawn on every
     afterRender, so they follow pan and zoom.
   - Seed nodes are drawn at twice their size; the label is forced and
     boxed (highlighted).
2. src/front/static/query/css/query-sigmagraph.css
   .sg-seed-halo-layer (no pointer events) and .sg-seed-halo (brand-red ring
   with a pulse; static under prefers-reduced-motion).
3. tests/units/front/test_explorer_seed_halo.py
   New contract tests for the render hook, the positioning inputs and the
   styles.

Checked in headless Chrome with Sigma 3.0.2: the ring stays centred on the
seed after a camera move.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
- src/front/static/query/css/query-sigmagraph.css
- tests/units/front/test_explorer_seed_halo.py (new)
